 "title": "Tell the Story of Why You Built Your Business",
 "topic": "content creation",
 "summary": "The creator suggests that before explaining what a business does, you should tell the story of why you decided things needed to be done differently. Instead of boring company history, focus on the genuine moments that bothered you in your industry, helping prospective clients remember and choose your business.",
 "key_points": [
  "Skip the usual boring company history about passion for excellence and customer service in 2012.",
  "Share the moment you recognized something in your industry that bothered you enough to act.",
  "Example problems: clients overwhelmed by choices, clients paying premium prices but chasing providers for info, or providers ignoring the client experience.",
  "Complete this sentence as a tip: One of the reasons I started doing things differently was because I got tired of seeing...",
  "The story does not need to be dramatic, it just needs to be genuine.",
  "Sharing what you believe should be different gives prospective clients a reason to remember and choose your business."
 ],
 "content": "Before you explain what your business does, there’s a story you should consider telling first. It’s the story of why you decided things needed to be done differently. Now, I’m not talking about the usual company history. We start in two thousand 12 with a passion for excellence and a commitment to customer service blah blah blah. Nobody gets particularly excited about that. I’m talking about the moment when you recognize something in your industry that bothered you enough to do something about it. So, for example, maybe you notice that clients were constantly being overwhelmed with choices when what they really wanted was a thoughtful recommendation or maybe you saw people paying premium prices but still having to chase their providers for information or perhaps you realize that everyone was so focused on delivering a particular service that nobody was paying attention to the experience that clients were having along the way. So, now you’ve got the beginning of an interesting story. You saw a problem, you believe there was a better way and you built your business around doing something about it. Now, here’s a tip. Complete this sentence. One of the reasons I started doing things differently was because I got tired of seeing than tell the story. It doesn’t need to be dramatic, it just needs to be genuine because when perspective clients understand what you believe should be different about your industry, they have a reason to remember your business and if they share that belief, they may have a compelling reason to choose you. So, if you’d like to learn how to build a more distinctive brand that specifically focuses on affluent clients, comment brand and I will send you information about my video program, The Ultimate Branding Blueprint. So, that’s comment brand to get information about that. This is Mark Satterfield. Hope you found this helpful. I’ll talk to you soon. Bye for now.",
